+    <details class="about" id="why">
+      <summary>Why am I seeing this? (for maintainers who got a reminder)</summary>
+      <p>Someone in the OWASP community used Bumper to check on your repository. Bumper lists every repository in the <a href="https://github.com/OWASP">OWASP GitHub organization</a> and ranks the idle ones. Each reminder is an ordinary GitHub issue that a person read and submitted under their own account, on your repository's own issue tracker. Nothing is sent anywhere else.</p>
+      <h3>How does Bumper decide a repository is a "project"?</h3>
+      <p>It doesn't decide OWASP project status; <a href="https://owasp.org/projects/">owasp.org/projects</a> does. Bumper only labels what it can see on GitHub:</p>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Project</strong>: the repository's GitHub homepage (<em>About → Website</em>) is its owasp.org project page, for example <code>https://owasp.org/projects/ctf-in-a-box</code>.</li>
+        <li><strong>Project site</strong>: an owasp.org project website repository (<code>www-project-…</code>).</li>
+        <li><strong>Chapter</strong>: a chapter website repository (<code>www-chapter-…</code>).</li>
+        <li><strong>Repo</strong>: anything not linked to a project page yet.</li>
+      </ul>
+      <h3>How do I change it or opt out?</h3>
+      <ul>
+        <li><strong>Link your repository to your project:</strong> set its GitHub homepage to your owasp.org project page. Bumper picks it up on its next daily refresh.</li>
+        <li><strong>Still active?</strong> Reply on the reminder and close it. A commit also resets the clock.</li>
+        <li><strong>Finished or moved?</strong> Archive the repository; archived repositories never get reminders.</li>
+        <li><strong>Don't want reminders at all?</strong> Add the topic <code>bumper-ignore</code> to the repository.</li>
+      </ul>
+      <p>Questions or a wrong mapping: <a href="https://git.owaspblt.org/BLT/issues">open an issue on the BLT forge</a> or ask in #project-blt on OWASP Slack.</p>
